WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.558
Step nine assembles the period for
the ISSO, from the twenty-eighth

2
00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:08.575
to the thirtieth of October, with
the A I inventory's vintage.

3
00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.725
It exits two.

4
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:12.717
The chain has no breaks
and no coverage gaps,

5
00:00:12.717 --> 00:00:17.287
across two packages, with nineteen
findings opened and one closed.

6
00:00:17.287 --> 00:00:18.888
But complete is false.

7
00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:23.749
The summary's controls table shows why:
some chapters haven't sent their findings.

8
00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:28.237
A C two is evidence incomplete
without Chapter 3's findings.

9
00:00:28.237 --> 00:00:33.438
I A five waits on Chapters 4 and 6,
and I A nine on Chapters 5 and 8.

10
00:00:33.438 --> 00:00:37.663
The other controls read evidence
present, the assessor decides.

11
00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:41.938
That's honest: an incomplete period
says so, instead of passing.

12
00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:44.352
The summary also has a Gate 7 table,

13
00:00:44.352 --> 00:00:47.800
and a row for each package
with its manifest hash.

14
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.230
The identity governance officer signs it.
